{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791802282,"nonce":"yDE+oSQr36FPbYkOalGqfnhkLFw=","message":"Audit associated with e8a1b50; NumberInput implemented in ffc482f.\n\nHighest priority: Input, Select and Combobox. None exposes control Size; their CSS fixes height/padding/type, and Combobox additionally fixes its chevron size. They should share size metrics for aligned form rows while preserving existing core input/select and Command behavior.\n\nNext: Textarea and InputOtp. Textarea needs padding/type/min-height density while retaining explicit width/height and wrapping behavior. InputOtp needs coordinated slot width/height, gap, separator, typography and overlaid editable field sizing.\n\nThen: Checkbox, RadioGroup, Slider and Badge. Checkbox/radio visual markers, labels/gaps and hit areas should scale together; RadioGroup should pass size to items. Slider track, thumb, label/value typography and pointer travel must remain aligned. Badge needs proportional type/padding/line-height instead of application-specific custom sizing.\n\nExisting size variants: Button, Toggle/ToggleGroup, ToggleSwitch, Tabs, Avatar/AvatarGroup, Progress, Spinner, Breadcrumb, Pagination and Kbd. Dialog/Sheet/Drawer sizes already describe panel dimensions rather than control density.\n\nSeparate density candidates: Table rows/cells, Accordion triggers/content spacing, TreeView rows, and menu/Command rows. Calendar could use day-cell/header density as a coordinated whole. These merit density APIs rather than resizing all container geometry indiscriminately. No additional component APIs changed in this audit.","files":null}]}